
|process-map[asf-processes]
  :title The meta-processes of ASF, as a system
  :created 2026-07-07
  :version 0.0.1
  :status first-pass

  ; A MECE-ish list of the processes that run (or should run), in mild hierarchy. Correct the carve freely.

  ; Conventions:
    - Each process carries a `health` tag (from findings) and a `drain` tag.
    - `drain` values:
      | healing    (steady-state, self-clearing if given a trigger + "do-one-extra" rule)
      | task-force (a one-off is the right fit; a steady rhythm would mis-fit)
      | nil        (not a backlog-shaped process)

    - A `?` marks a genuinely unknown sub-process we'd have to design.
    - Signal-flow is noted per-item as fed-by / feeds, and drawn only for the
      core loop, where it clarifies the dynamics.

  |meta-meta-process[self-governance]
    :name How this map governs and evolves itself
    :source-sink participant-feedback

    Kept to a few imperatives on purpose:
    - Make it easy to follow the *right current* process, or to reach for the
      tool around it.
    - Make it just as easy to *evolve* a process — incrementally, or more
      fundamentally.
    - Every participant may give feedback and ideas on *any* process.
    - That participant feedback is the *only* source/sink point of the
      meta-process itself.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; THE SPINE -- cross-cutting, not a stage
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[spine]
    :name Decision-routing & stewardship
    :scope cross-cutting

    Every stall below reduces to a decision that never reached Joseph in
    actionable form; this is the parent, not a sibling (cluster 02's insight).

    |process[decision-surfacing]
      :name Decision surfacing
      :health broken
      :drain healing
      :example spikes/epistemic-target-ontology/

      Recognize a genuine-Joseph fork, assemble a real brief (reconstructed
      context + options + recommendation + honest uncertainty + the actual
      pointer), route it to a valve he can act from. JOSEPH-TODO catches under
      half (`<½`); the newer half leaks. Per-fork trigger + prune. The worked
      example that already exists is `spikes/epistemic-target-ontology/`.

    |process[coherence-stewardship]?
      :name Coherence stewardship (the domain-master role)
      :health absent
      :drain nil
      :design-unknown how it's instantiated across turnover

      Not a gatekeeper; a check on cross-process coherence who can say "hold that
      integration until the intro lands," "these two pull opposite ways — make
      them read each other first." A standing role, not a queue.

    |process[valve]
      :name The valve itself (JOSEPH-TODO)
      :health under-fed
      :drain healing

      The durable list of genuinely-his calls. Exists, well-designed,
      under-fed.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; GENERATION (sources)
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[generation]
    :name Generation (sources)

    |process[spike-lifecycle]
      :name Spike lifecycle
      :health healthy
      :drain nil
      :feeds [verification integration]

      Launch → derive → refute-verify → land self-contained at honest tier. It's
      a source, not a queue.

    |process[spike-proposals]
      :name Spike-proposal generation
      :health whim-triggered
      :drain nil
      :feeds [spike-lifecycle proposals-lifecycle]

      "What's missing / what could be transformative" → proposals. When run, it
      floods downstream.

    |process[ideation-surfacing]
      :name Gap / ideation surfacing
      :health latent
      :drain nil
      :feeds [spike-lifecycle spike-proposals]

      From Working Notes, theory walks, open questions. Latent, no rhythm.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; VERIFICATION
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[verification]
    :name Verification

    |process[de-novo-audits]
      :name De-novo audits (open-ended, multi-model, low-prescription)
      :health strong
      :drain healing
      :fed-by [integration]
      :feeds [integration]

      The crown-jewel method; each establishes **lower bounds** (found problems),
      never completeness. Strong method, but no cadence/trigger and no
      "already-audited" summary handed in; coverage is uneven — test the
      low-mean-Poisson heatmap hypothesis. Fed by edits, feeds findings.

    |process[follow-up-audits]?
      :name Follow-up / triggered audits
      :health absent
      :drain healing
      :design-unknown the trigger + the scoped-instruction generator

      Fired by an edit, especially multi-segment edits (most are), possibly with
      specialized instructions. **Does not exist** — a named gap.

    |process[independent-verification]
      :name Independent verification / refute-cadence
      :health healthy
      :drain nil

      Confirmer ≠ author on load-bearing landings.

    |process[empirical-verification]?
      :name Simulation / empirical verification
      :health absent
      :drain task-force
      :wire-to [vivarium relata papers]
      :design-unknown the whole empirical/sim discipline

      Sims/experiments/benchmarks as first-class, with knowledge landing
      self-contained + the artifact externally-citable at publication. **No
      disciplined process** (a Joseph canary); 11 tst `.py` parked since March.
      Task-force to inventory, then healing. Wire to `vivarium`
      (identifiability-by-construction lab), `relata` (citable artifact), and the
      submitted papers.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; INTEGRATION (the queues that back up)
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[integration]
    :name Integration

    |process[finding-routing]
      :name Audit-finding routing (strengthen-first)
      :health healthy
      :drain healing
      :fed-by [verification]
      :feeds [audit-graduation canon valve proposals-lifecycle]

      Route, don't execute; disposition per finding. Routing is healthy.

    |process[audit-graduation]
      :name Audit graduation / working-dir clearing
      :health broken
      :drain task-force

      Verify dispositions + settle gold → git-mv + MANIFEST. Broken: 0/22, the
      gold-dir gate never convened. Task-force to clear the 22, then healing once
      the gate becomes a standing policy.

    |process[spike-integration]
      :name Spike integration
      :health healthy
      :drain healing

      Land the knowledge, route the artifact.

    |process[reflection-harvest]
      :name Audit Reflections Harvest
      :health stalled
      :drain healing
      :feeds [pedagogy-pipeline]

      The pedagogically-valuable in-order reflections. Stalled **and**
      mis-routed. Correction: this routes to **pedagogy**, not Working Notes;
      healing once re-aimed.

    |process[sibling-backport]
      :name Sibling back-integration
      :health broken
      :drain healing
      :fed-by [neighborhood-metabolism]

      Results from neurips / vestigia / vivarium / embeddings / causal-language
      that are sharper than canon. Broken — backport debt is the neighborhood's
      central metabolic failure. Healing per-result, plus one task-force for the
      standing NeurIPS Phase-A.

    |process[conflict-reconciliation]?
      :name Integration-conflict reconciliation
      :health absent
      :drain nil
      :design-unknown the reconciliation mechanism

      Two landings pulling different ways read each other and opine before either
      lands. Barely exists — the PROPOSALS knot is its absence. Drain nil: it's
      the coherence-role acting, not a queue.

    |process[proposals-lifecycle]
      :name PROPOSALS lifecycle
      :health stalled
      :drain task-force
      :fed-by [spike-proposals]
      :feeds [spine]

      Big architectural moves; overlapping, conflicting, whole-theory-affecting.
      Grossly stalled/knotted. **Task-force** to untangle the existing knot (a
      steady rhythm mis-fits a tangled backlog), then healing.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; COHERENCE MAINTENANCE
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[coherence]
    :name Coherence maintenance

    |process[lexicon]
      :name Naming / terminology / lexicon
      :health infra-healthy, decision-stalled
      :drain healing
      :feeds [spine]

      Infra (bin/term) healthy; ~506 currents unrouted; LEXICON reorg blocked.
      Route N/cycle + drain.

    |process[drift-repair]
      :name Cross-segment consistency / drift repair
      :health opportunistic
      :drain healing

      Idiom-drift, stale cross-refs.

    |process[navigator-currency]
      :name OUTLINE / navigator currency
      :health stale-prone
      :drain healing

      Status columns vs frontmatter; "missing" markers. Recurs; a lint that
      cross-checks would make it self-clearing.

    |process[working-note-drain]
      :name Working-Note discipline / drain
      :health broken
      :drain task-force

      The deluge — 95% of segments; Gate-4 never fires. Healing *if* a drain is
      defined (see the promotion-terminus decision), plus one task-force to clear
      the existing pool.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; COMPREHENSIBILITY / PEDAGOGY
  ; "not a monster to those who need it most" -- first-class
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[pedagogy]
    :name Comprehensibility / pedagogy

    |process[pedagogy-pipeline]
      :name Reflection-gold -> pedagogy pipeline (Joseph-as-test)
      :health nascent
      :drain healing
      :fed-by [reflection-harvest model-of-joseph]

      Harvested gold tested against the real reader.

    |process[mental-model-authoring]
      :name Mental-model-first authoring (Feynman-brief / bathtub-bar)
      :health aspirational
      :drain healing

      Framing prose written as an in-order walk, not a from-above artifact.

    |process[reader-model]
      :name Reader-model-of-Joseph maintenance
      :see model-of-joseph

      This is where the reader-model *feeds*; the build lives in model-of-joseph.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; RELEASE / DISSEMINATION -- separate from truth, per Joseph
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[release]
    :name Release / dissemination

    |process[monograph-build]
      :name Monograph build
      :health healthy
      :drain nil

      Markdown-first, four volumes.

    |process[citation-discipline]
      :name Citation / bibliography discipline
      :health architecture landed, migration stalled
      :drain healing

      relata-wired; per-segment migration owner-gated. Healing per-volume.

    |process[archival-release]
      :name Archival release (Zenodo)
      :health stale
      :drain task-force

      Frozen at v0.1.0. Task-force per release point (a Joseph-gated act).

    |process[paper-submission]
      :name Paper authoring / submission
      :see neighborhood-metabolism

      Mostly in sibling repos.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; GOVERNANCE / META -- processes that keep processes healthy (meta-SOPs)
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[governance]
    :name Governance / meta

    |process[governing-doc-integrity]
      :name Governing-doc integrity
      :health broken
      :drain task-force

      CLAUDE.md-as-amplifier; review cadence + generate-what's-derivable. Broken:
      F6 unowned since May. Task-force for the first audit, then healing cadence.

    |process[memory-curation]
      :name Memory curation
      :health mixed
      :drain healing

      Project (healthy), global + memorata workshop (frozen ~8 wks). Healing,
      plus a task-force to resume the frozen arc or consciously set it down.

    |process[tracker-architecture]
      :name Tracker / SOP architecture
      :health design-problem
      :drain task-force

      The SOP-shift pattern applied to the TODO/tracker layer: parallel zones,
      digestible sizes, PRACTICA as index, CHANGELOG as drain, move-finished-out.
      Overlaps the `practica` project as the eventual tool; a candidate for
      non-markdown. This *is* the design problem itself — task-force to design +
      first migration, then healing.

    |process[harness-provisioning]
      :name Tooling / harness provisioning
      :health under-used
      :drain healing
      :gated-on .claude/ un-gitignore call

      Hooks, project subagents, worktrees, schedules, agentic-reading
      scaffolding. Out-invented the harness cognitively, under-used it
      mechanically.

    |process[repo-hygiene]
      :name Repo-shape / packaging hygiene
      :health broken
      :drain task-force

      The monolith-*illusion* (theory is 8.6M of 225M; ref/_obs/mono weight).
      One-time cleanup, orthogonal to decomposition.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; CROSS-PROJECT FLOWS (feeders in/out)
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[cross-project]
    :name Cross-project flows

    |process[neighborhood-metabolism]
      :name Neighborhood metabolism
      :health outward healthy, return broken
      :drain healing
      :feeds [sibling-backport]

      Outward concept-flow (healthy) vs return backport-flow (broken → sibling
      back-integration); the bridge-authoring template (vivarium ASF.md) is not
      propagated.

    |process[external-input]?
      :name External input
      :health mixed
      :design-unknown theory-news monitoring

      Human review (Alan Walton PR pending) exists; theory-news monitoring does
      not exist.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; INTERLIMINAL -- always-on in any Joseph dialog, deliberately NOT DAG-wired
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[interliminal]
    :name Interliminal
    :note always-on, deliberately not DAG-wired

    |process[model-of-joseph]?
      :name Model-of-Joseph
      :health nascent
      :drain healing
      :feeds [pedagogy-pipeline spine]
      :design-unknown the model-of-Joseph build

      The reader-model, plus turning agents' instinctive resonance-detection into
      recorded, accumulating knowledge. Just seeded (global memory). "General
      agent modeling of Joseph" is added as a process to design — same shape:
      stop the leakage (lost detections), heal the backlog (comb the dialog
      logs). Drain healing (probe-and-record).

    |process[peer-voice-calibration]
      :name Model-of-other / peer-voice calibration
      :health healthy
      :drain nil

      The delegation register. A standing discipline.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; THE CORE LOOP -- where signal-flow clarifies the dynamics
  ; ==========================================================================

  |diagram[core-loop]
    :caption The core loop
    !:text:
        generation --> verification --> integration --> [files change]
            ^                                                |
            |                                                v
            +----------------- triggers <----------- follow-up audit
                                                             |
        PROPOSALS <-- ideation      siblings <-- metabolism  |
            |                                                v
            |                                           coherence
            +--------> THE SPINE (decision-routing) <---------+
                              |
                       pedagogy <-- model-of-Joseph
                              |
                       release (from the stabilized corpus)

  |diagnosis
    **The diagnosis in one sentence:** these are **un-clocked queues driven by a
    single human clock** — sources (spikes, proposals, audits) fire on Joseph's
    whim, so a burst of generation floods verification/integration, whose
    *drains* (graduation, routing-to-Joseph) are also gated on Joseph, who is
    whim-clocked too; so everything backs up between his sessions.

  |fix-shape :attribution Joseph
    **The fix shape (his):** give each process a **trigger** (≥1 queued item =
    work), **weave healing** into steady-state (drain-one-extra ⇒ backlog → 0 by
    construction), and **reduce the human-clocked part** to genuine theory-domain
    decisions, each arriving as a real brief. Reserve **task-forces** only where a
    backlog is tangled or one-off (audit-graduation's 22 dirs, the PROPOSALS knot,
    the Working-Note pool, the tracker-architecture design, the repo-hygiene
    cleanup) — everywhere else, healing beats a task-force.

  |open-unknowns
    :items [follow-up-audits empirical-verification conflict-reconciliation coherence-stewardship external-input tracker-architecture model-of-joseph]

    The `?` items still to design: the follow-up-audit trigger +
    scoped-instruction generator · the empirical/sim discipline · the
    integration-conflict mechanism · the coherence-steward role across turnover ·
    theory-news monitoring · the tracker-architecture itself · the model-of-Joseph
    build.

  |unplaced
    :name Deferred until the theory reaches it (Joseph, 2026-07-07)
    The ELI / `_core` / empirical-cohort operational substrate — left undefined
    on purpose until the theory gets there. Its processes get carved when the
    theory does, not before.
